                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b7811f86-1686-3d17-954c-fce2c05c2ca5",
                        "entry_id": "3aca905d-7019-3306-8ee4-a7dcc256a09a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. то же, что монах"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "461acbbd-0929-4080-9edc-5649acab8fbc",
                                "sense_id": "b7811f86-1686-3d17-954c-fce2c05c2ca5",
                                "text": "Как и чем существовал чернец Федос в своей тюрьме от половины октября до конца января 1726 года, — неизвестно, но в конце января архангельский губернатор Измайлов приехал в корельский монастырь и приказал перевести узника в другую тюрьму: Феодосий был так слаб, что не мог ходить, и его перенесли на руках, а 5 февраля караульный фендрих Григорьев рапортовал губернатору, что чернец Федос умер."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1df356b8-b3b2-4d98-9a64-18efb6579e05",
                                "sense_id": "b7811f86-1686-3d17-954c-fce2c05c2ca5",
                                "text": "Неподалеку отсюда есть монастырь, Княж-Хабаров называется; живет в нем чернец Софронушка."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9c2c0758-64a4-4816-8886-09d7856cdb2b",
                        "source_entry_id": "3aca905d-7019-3306-8ee4-a7dcc256a09a",
                        "source_sense_id": "b7811f86-1686-3d17-954c-fce2c05c2ca5",
                        "target_lang_word": "monk",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "monk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a87a4d4-2741-3d1b-8e91-1178520e5fda",
                                        "entry_id": "057fda98-71de-327a-b80d-21a8ba0e681f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male member of a monastic order who has devoted his life for religious service."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5b83562-8a5d-4dd3-a363-e97a7cf8e0c0",
                                                "sense_id": "3a87a4d4-2741-3d1b-8e91-1178520e5fda",
                                                "text": "This is believed to be the completeſt liſt of this voluminous, proſaick, and driveling monk, that can be formed, without acceſs, at leaſt, to every manuſcript library in the kingdom, which would be very difficult, if not imposſible, to obtain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf12177b-0553-455a-b0c1-cca17c9f77a8",
                                                "sense_id": "3a87a4d4-2741-3d1b-8e91-1178520e5fda",
                                                "text": "In clusters on the plain, like cowlless monks at matins, sat the vultures that had settled on the corpse of the hyena impaled by the female rhino […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a2e776ec-84a6-3ed5-9141-a12608fe8c32",
                                        "entry_id": "057fda98-71de-327a-b80d-21a8ba0e681f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In earlier usage, an eremite or hermit devoted to solitude, as opposed to a cenobite, who lived communally."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46738419-da33-49f2-b9ad-b2494773ca08",
                                                "sense_id": "a2e776ec-84a6-3ed5-9141-a12608fe8c32",
                                                "text": "Tony's face expressed relief, and Nettie sat silent for a moment until the vicar said “It was a generous impulse, but it may have been a momentary one, while in the case of monk and crusader there must have been a sustaining purpose, and possibly a great abnegation, a leaving of lands and possessions.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "973e8745-a679-39f8-a660-ca5eebd079b4",
                                        "entry_id": "057fda98-71de-327a-b80d-21a8ba0e681f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who leads an isolated life; a loner, a hermit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f46f84e-4b3a-3021-86fb-fdc375886a55",
                                        "entry_id": "057fda98-71de-327a-b80d-21a8ba0e681f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An unmarried man who does not have sexual relationships."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a6526c56-890c-3028-b59a-bb4be14af250",
                                        "entry_id": "057fda98-71de-327a-b80d-21a8ba0e681f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A judge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
